data.content:
Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Generic template rendering with Move Up/Down buttons per item.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — Code-behind with:
- `Items` parameter copied to a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the original).
- `OnOrderChanged` fires after each swap, passing a read-only copy of the reordered list.
- Buttons are disabled at boundaries (first item can't move up, last can't move down).

Usage matches your example — just use `OnOrderChanged` to receive the new order:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { /* ... */ };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
